    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d178">

                <pb facs="0265" n="245" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v12p2/pg245"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">756D.5 MSP/1–452: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 178<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Indonesia (Cochran) to
                        the Department of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >confidential<lb/>priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Djakarta</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-01-04T15:00:00+07:30">January 4, 1952—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>952. For State and ECA. With agreement Indo FonMin Subardjo, I handed him 11:30
                    today Emb note Nr. 182 dated Jan 4<anchor n="2" xml:id="d178-f1"/> in exact
                    terms set forth Dept A–110 Nov 23<anchor n="3" xml:id="d178-f2"/> with fol
                    exceptions: <list>
                        <label>(a)</label>
                        <item>Point 3 of para 1 omitted.</item>
                        <label>(b)</label>
                        <item>Words “economic and mil” removed from point 6 para 1.</item>
                        <label>(c)</label>
                        <item>Sub-para of para 1 renumbered 1 to 5 inclusive after elimination
                            original point 3.</item>
                        <label>(d)</label>
                        <item>Para 4 reads as follows: “Govt of Indo considers that econ cooperation
                            agreement between Govt of Indo and Govt US, signed Djakarta Oct 16,
                                1950,<anchor n="4" xml:id="d178-f3"/> has been and will continue to
                            be binding obligation of Repub of Indo, according its terms, pending
                            Parliament action.”</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>Explained to FonMin he shld give me note prior Jan 8 indicating that provisions
                    my note acceptable his govt. Will report promptly upon receipt thereof.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cochran</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d178-f1" n="2" xml:id="d178-f1-content">
                <p>For text, see Department of State Treaties and Other International Acts Series
                    (TIAS) No. 2762 or <hi rendition="#italic">United States Treaties and Other
                        International Agreements</hi> (UST), vol. 4, p. 21. Achmad Subardjo was the
                    Indonesian Foreign Minister.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d178-f2" n="3" xml:id="d178-f2-content">
                <p>For text, see <ref target="frus1951v06p1#pg_729"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, 1951, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">vi</hi>, Part 1,
                        p. 729</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d178-f3" n="4" xml:id="d178-f3-content">
                <p>This agreement is not printed; for text of a press release issued on the occasion
                    of the signing of the agreement, see Department of State <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bulletin</hi>, Oct. 30, 1950, p. 702.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
